rder-line/50 last:border-0\",\"children\":[\"$L1d\",\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\",\"$L20\"]}],\"$L21\"]}]]}]]}],\"$L22\"]}]]}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base font-semibold text-ink mb-4\",\"children\":\"Builder notes\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line\",\"children\":\"The D25 is a larger cousin to the D19, D21, and D22 cases, offering just over 8L of space while accommodating a Founder's Edition RTX 3070. The case design is simple and allows for efficient air flow without fine mesh. The Jginyue B650I Night Devil motherboard performed well despite not being rated for CPUs over 105w TDP. The Ryzen 7 7700 CPU was power efficient at 90w max draw and paired well with the RTX 3070 for 1440p gaming. The ID-Cooling SE-207-SE cooler maintained excellent thermals throughout all workloads. Build time was approximately 20 minutes. Case panel quality is decent but thin, requiring careful handling. No dedicated top or bottom fan support in this configuration, but airflow remains adequate with the 92mm Noctua exhaust fan. This is a good productivity and gaming system in a compact form factor. Case requires regular cleaning due to lack of fine mesh filtration.\"}]]}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-5 space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base font-semibold text-ink\",\"children\":\"Performance\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-ink-muted uppercase tracking-wide font-medium mb-1\",\"children\":\"CPU — CB23 Multi\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-ink tabular-nums\",\"children\":\"18,433\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2 mt-1.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{